%N A399655 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of tilings of an n X k rectangle by tetrominoes with no edge-adjacent tiles of the same free type, 1 <= k <= n.
%C A399655 Rotations and reflections of individual tiles are allowed. The five free tetromino types are I, O, T, L (including J), and S (including Z).
%C A399655 Two distinct tiles are edge-adjacent if they share at least one unit-length boundary edge. Contact at a vertex is allowed.
%C A399655 Tilings are counted on a fixed rectangle; rotations and reflections of a tiling are counted separately when they give different partitions of the board.
%C A399655 A230031 is the corresponding unrestricted tetromino tiling array, read by antidiagonals.
%C A399655 For each fixed k, the generating function Sum_{n>=0} T(n,k)*x^n, with T(0,k)=1, is rational: a finite transfer matrix records the tile types in a bounded frontier.
%H A399655 Meghanto Majumder, <a href="/A399655/b399655.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..78</a>
%H A399655 Liang Kai, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.17698">Solving tiling enumeration problems by tensor network contractions</a>, arXiv:2503.17698 [math.CO], 2025.
%H A399655 Meghanto Majumder, <a href="/A399655/a399655.png">All 50 tetromino tilings with no edge-adjacent tiles of the same free type for the 4 X 6 rectangle</a>.
%H A399655 Meghanto Majumder, <a href="/A399655/a399655.txt">Python program calculating T(n,k)</a>.
%H A399655 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetromino">Tetromino</a>.
%F A399655 T(n,k) = 0 if n*k mod 4 > 0. (reverse is not true, see T(4,2))
%e A399655 T(2,2)=1: a single O-tetromino covers the board.
%e A399655 T(4,2)=0: all four unrestricted tilings of the 4 X 2 rectangle have two edge-adjacent tiles of the same free type.
%e A399655 T(4,3)=2. The two tilings are shown with 3 rows and 4 columns. A and B are distinct L-tetrominoes, and C is an S-type tetromino. The two L-tiles do not share an edge:
%e A399655    A A C B    A C B B
%e A399655    A C C B    A C C B
%e A399655    A C B B    A A C B
%e A399655 The triangle T(n,k) begins:
%e A399655   0;
%e A399655   0, 1;
%e A399655   0, 0,  0;
%e A399655   1, 0,  2,   8;
%e A399655   0, 0,  0,  22,    0;
%e A399655   0, 0,  0,  50,    0,  316;
%e A399655   0, 0,  0,  82,    0,    0,     0;
%e A399655   0, 0, 82,  84, 1284, 5864, 39456, 271544;
%e A399655   ...
